{"title":"Order of operations","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>order of operations</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_convention\" title=\"Mathematical convention\">mathematical convention</a> for the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Computation (page does not exist)\">computation</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic\" title=\"Arithmetic\">arithmetic</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Expression\" title=\"Expression\">expressions</a>.  The below list indicates the order to do <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Operation\" title=\"Operation\">operations</a>, from top to bottom.\n</p>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parentheses\" title=\"Parentheses\">Parentheses</a> -- when there are multiple operations and parentheses within the parentheses, treat the expression inside as a separate expression and do the order of operations within said parentheses.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Exponent\" title=\"Exponent\">Exponents</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiplication\" title=\"Multiplication\">Multiplication</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Division\" title=\"Division\">Division</a> -- done from left to right</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition\" title=\"Addition\">Addition</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction\" title=\"Subtraction\">Subtraction</a> -- done from left to right</li></ol>\n<p>The order of operations is usually summarized by the acronym PEMDAS. An AoPS mnemonic you can use to remember the order of operations is \"Please Evaluate, My Dear AoPS Students\".\n</p><p>Sometimes, properties like the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Communicative_Property&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Communicative Property (page does not exist)\">Communicative Property</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Associative_Property&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Associative Property (page does not exist)\">Associative Property</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distributive_Property\" title=\"Distributive Property\">Distributive Property</a> can be applied.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Example_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Example_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#External_Links\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">External Links</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_1\">Example 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Example 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c5a3e0eb4893c6db4b734a4a72d0ce68669c45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8-(3+5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"19\" />.  First, we do addition first because it is in parentheses.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b3871c41ac5d9f834c2f59b21cc6f0314e90fb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^8-8\\]\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />\nNext, we evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1635abf3f228d02f20315b199c17f21dc0a49ccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> because exponents go next.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b5728ef5db4ccf3e774bd2a9ef6aa6cf6950d341.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[256-8\\]\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />\nAfterward, there are no multiplication and division, so we can move on to addition and subtraction.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbab2d064fe6ffdc9353fecf1b13e8aa7b58276.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[248\\]\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea2f56ee488dd6f62635ba149c0153c133f2624b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8-(3+5) = \\boxed{248}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"158\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_2\">Example 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Example 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e030f513285758beb870cb47a13d72cdcd772f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14(4\\times 7-58)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />.  The operations in the parentheses go first, but there are subtraction and multiplication both involved.  Within the parentheses, the multiplication goes first, then the subtraction.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e1b80b783beef9eda787128dc65d7bce2f0a73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14(28-58)-1\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04fce9716f87d1839e3d1faaade3666d106faa90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14(-30)-1\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />\nAfterward, we do multiplication, then subtraction.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542eca4f53aff72a8328679802b2bba20f1658e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-420-1\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34b5e53627e4ea817a268510d004245b8994585.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-421\\]\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078945fa7a87f8ba4c7cdd8aaf747b0058a31f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14(4\\times 7-58)-1 = \\boxed{-421}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"221\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic\" title=\"Arithmetic\">Arithmetic</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"External_Links\">External Links</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: External Links\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/Ti9nA3Tn_CE\">Video</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Order_of_operations&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022848\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 96/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2033/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.755      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.755      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5036:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022848 and revision id 260822. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}